0..77 Comment "// The data subject\'s shared declarations, written once and imported by every"
78..155 Comment "// source that reads them (`import \"./data-base.gandr\";`): the free naturals,"
156..231 Comment "// their addition and the numerals two and three, the integers presented by"
232..308 Comment "// two cancelling constructors, a three-colour enumeration, the two branches"
309..384 Comment "// of a binary node and the polymorphic lists. A data block is an inductive"
385..462 Comment "// type given by its constructors (Martin-Löf, _Intuitionistic Type Theory_,"
463..535 Comment "// Bibliopolis, 1984), and a rule between constructor terms quotients it"
536..596 Comment "// (Altenkirch et al., _Quotient inductive-inductive types_,"
597..634 Comment "// doi:10.1007/978-3-319-89366-2_16)."
635..709 Comment "// The universe subject reads the naturals and the branches from here too."
711..778 Comment "/// Natural numbers, free: every constructor term is its own value."
